1
00:00:06,080 --> 00:00:07,120
(This series is a fictional work created
for entertainment purposes.)

2
00:00:07,200 --> 00:00:08,240
(The characters, events, locations, organizations
agencies, as well as religions, beliefs)

3
00:00:08,320 --> 00:00:09,280
(and symbols appearing in this story
are presented for storytelling purposes only.)

4
00:00:09,360 --> 00:00:10,120
(No intention is made to reference, imply, criticize)

5
00:00:10,200 --> 00:00:10,960
(or allude to any individual,
organization or religious group)

6
00:00:14,480 --> 00:00:15,480
(Chat)

7
00:00:15,560 --> 00:00:20,520
Hey

8
00:00:23,360 --> 00:00:24,200
(Seungwoo)

9
00:00:24,280 --> 00:00:27,000
I thought I wouldn't be able to live without you

10
00:00:27,080 --> 00:00:30,480
But look at me now

11
00:00:30,800 --> 00:00:32,360
I'm shining

12
00:00:32,439 --> 00:00:34,160
On nights when the sky turns against me

13
00:00:34,240 --> 00:00:37,200
When the rain falls inside my heart

14
00:00:37,280 --> 00:00:38,240
I play the same old songs

15
00:00:38,320 --> 00:00:40,560
That we used to listen to together

16
00:00:40,640 --> 00:00:42,320
Your picture is still right there

17
00:00:42,400 --> 00:00:44,120
But I'm not crying anymore

18
00:00:44,200 --> 00:00:45,120
I used to want you so badly

19
00:00:45,200 --> 00:00:46,800
Now I'm beginning to understand

20
00:00:46,880 --> 00:00:49,520
That love comes and go

21
00:00:49,600 --> 00:00:51,560
I thought my whole world had to fall apart

22
00:00:51,640 --> 00:00:52,480
But in the end

23
00:00:52,560 --> 00:00:55,960
It was just my heart learning how to move on

24
00:00:57,240 --> 00:00:59,640
I used to say "Can't live without you"

25
00:00:59,720 --> 00:01:02,280
But today, I can proudly say, I'm cool

26
00:01:02,360 --> 00:01:03,480
I’m looking so good

27
00:01:03,560 --> 00:01:05,960
Damn I don’t even try to do

28
00:01:23,080 --> 00:01:24,520
You must choose.

29
00:01:31,200 --> 00:01:32,400
What do you mean?

30
00:01:32,479 --> 00:01:33,920
You must choose

31
00:01:34,479 --> 00:01:35,720
and make good decisions

32
00:01:36,080 --> 00:01:38,479
both in work and in love.

33
00:01:38,560 --> 00:01:40,680
If it's about work, I can understand that.

34
00:01:41,200 --> 00:01:42,600
But when it comes to love,

35
00:01:42,680 --> 00:01:44,120
there’s no way I’ll change my mind.

36
00:01:44,200 --> 00:01:45,080
But

37
00:01:45,160 --> 00:01:48,000
you will let love get involved with work.

38
00:01:55,960 --> 00:01:57,800
There’s absolutely no way that will happen.

39
00:01:58,840 --> 00:02:00,160
Just be careful then.

40
00:02:00,240 --> 00:02:01,920
Because one single mistake

41
00:02:03,760 --> 00:02:05,680
will cause everything to fall apart.

42
00:02:14,720 --> 00:02:17,600
We spent 1 year developing this product.

43
00:02:17,680 --> 00:02:20,040
And to solve the pain point of regular sunscreen

44
00:02:20,120 --> 00:02:21,440
where you have to squeeze a tube,

45
00:02:21,520 --> 00:02:22,600
you just open the cap and

46
00:02:22,680 --> 00:02:24,360
you can spray it directly onto your face,

47
00:02:24,440 --> 00:02:26,200
and it can also be applied over makeup.

48
00:02:26,280 --> 00:02:28,400
Our formula contains mineral oil

49
00:02:28,480 --> 00:02:30,920
to add moisture to the skin of your face.

50
00:02:31,320 --> 00:02:32,920
And our product design emphasizes

51
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:34,360
a distinctive bottle color,

52
00:02:34,800 --> 00:02:35,640
just picking it up

53
00:02:35,720 --> 00:02:37,680
is enough to make our product memorable.

54
00:02:37,760 --> 00:02:39,079
Doesn’t this color

55
00:02:39,160 --> 00:02:40,800
look a little strange?

56
00:02:41,640 --> 00:02:43,320
We want to create brand recognition.

57
00:02:43,840 --> 00:02:45,680
First impressions are crucial.

58
00:02:45,760 --> 00:02:47,240
A bottle color like this

59
00:02:47,320 --> 00:02:48,160
draws people’s attention

60
00:02:48,240 --> 00:02:49,640
and makes it easy to share.

61
00:02:50,040 --> 00:02:51,840
I think this idea is quite interesting.

62
00:02:59,960 --> 00:03:02,720
Everyone, our team has a problem.

63
00:03:11,800 --> 00:03:13,840
Their idea is pretty brilliant though.

64
00:03:15,720 --> 00:03:16,560
Then...

65
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:19,520
let’s quickly find the weaknesses of this product.

66
00:03:19,600 --> 00:03:20,960
I will absolutely not let Team B

67
00:03:21,040 --> 00:03:22,720
beat our Team A.

68
00:03:26,720 --> 00:03:27,960
Here it is.

69
00:03:28,040 --> 00:03:29,160
Our team’s product.

70
00:03:29,240 --> 00:03:31,079
I’ve already updated everything.

71
00:03:32,840 --> 00:03:34,720
This is the latest update, right?

72
00:03:34,800 --> 00:03:37,040
Yes, and it’s all compiled together.

73
00:03:42,160 --> 00:03:43,680
And I think

74
00:03:43,760 --> 00:03:46,720
this product can become a top seller too

75
00:03:46,800 --> 00:03:47,880
because not many companies

76
00:03:47,960 --> 00:03:49,560
have a formula like this yet.

77
00:03:50,079 --> 00:03:51,520
And when do you plan to launch?

78
00:03:51,600 --> 00:03:53,120
Around three months.

79
00:03:56,400 --> 00:03:58,840
Excuse me, it's Cathy Doll company.

80
00:04:01,200 --> 00:04:03,200
When you say there’s no competition,

81
00:04:03,600 --> 00:04:05,200
where did you check that information from?

82
00:04:06,120 --> 00:04:09,000
From reliable industry reports.

83
00:04:09,440 --> 00:04:10,680
Then why is there information

84
00:04:10,760 --> 00:04:12,000
that Cathy Doll is currently

85
00:04:12,080 --> 00:04:13,520
developing this same product?

86
00:04:17,160 --> 00:04:18,839
Where did that information come from?

87
00:04:21,200 --> 00:04:23,040
The information came from Team A.

88
00:04:24,720 --> 00:04:26,520
Then go call Team A’s leader in.

89
00:04:34,600 --> 00:04:36,600
You are at risk of losing your job

90
00:04:36,680 --> 00:04:37,960
and your reputation.

91
00:04:38,840 --> 00:04:40,360
Compose yourself well

92
00:04:40,960 --> 00:04:42,880
and you will get through it.

93
00:05:01,080 --> 00:05:03,680
How confident are you in the information you found?

94
00:05:04,280 --> 00:05:05,520
I'm very confident.

95
00:05:05,600 --> 00:05:06,640
because Team A

96
00:05:06,720 --> 00:05:08,520
has been tracking competitor companies’ information,

97
00:05:09,160 --> 00:05:10,880
and regarding this particular product,

98
00:05:10,960 --> 00:05:13,920
there is clear information in the industry report.

99
00:05:20,480 --> 00:05:21,600
May I?

100
00:05:26,320 --> 00:05:27,240
Here you go.

101
00:05:31,880 --> 00:05:32,920
Here you go.

102
00:05:52,720 --> 00:05:54,440
But this is just a market trend

103
00:05:54,800 --> 00:05:56,200
it hasn’t actually been produced yet.

104
00:05:56,280 --> 00:05:58,200
But a contact who works at Cathy Doll,

105
00:05:58,280 --> 00:05:59,640
someone I’ve worked with before,

106
00:05:59,720 --> 00:06:01,560
told me that this product

107
00:06:01,640 --> 00:06:03,320
will be released next month.

108
00:06:07,160 --> 00:06:08,040
Even if they release first,

109
00:06:08,120 --> 00:06:09,360
if our product is truly good,

110
00:06:09,440 --> 00:06:10,920
customers will still choose us.

111
00:06:11,560 --> 00:06:13,800
When you didn’t even know about their product at all,

112
00:06:14,320 --> 00:06:16,200
how can you be confident yours will be better?

113
00:06:22,280 --> 00:06:24,480
VEGA lab has never followed behind anyone.

114
00:06:26,200 --> 00:06:28,280
I’m going to have to reconsider you lot.

115
00:06:52,920 --> 00:06:54,920
I won’t beat around the bush.

116
00:06:55,520 --> 00:06:58,640
Team B has only three months left.

117
00:07:00,160 --> 00:07:02,000
If there are still no results,

118
00:07:02,080 --> 00:07:03,480
I’ll have to let you go.

119
00:07:04,360 --> 00:07:05,840
I’ll take full responsibility.

120
00:07:06,360 --> 00:07:08,040
I mean the entire team.

121
00:07:49,159 --> 00:07:50,600
This lane is brutal.

122
00:07:51,480 --> 00:07:52,840
But I'm getting ganked right now.

123
00:07:52,920 --> 00:07:54,159
Can I get some support?

124
00:07:54,240 --> 00:07:55,760
Yeah, hold on.

125
00:07:55,840 --> 00:07:57,080
No, play properly.

126
00:07:58,960 --> 00:08:00,120
Hey!

127
00:08:01,920 --> 00:08:02,960
Be careful!

128
00:08:03,040 --> 00:08:04,160
Yeah, yeah.

129
00:08:05,280 --> 00:08:06,360
Yeah, yeah.

130
00:08:06,440 --> 00:08:07,840
Attack them.

131
00:08:14,840 --> 00:08:16,320
Use Troy for magic resist first,

132
00:08:16,400 --> 00:08:18,160
the other side has mages,

133
00:08:18,240 --> 00:08:19,440
they're strong.

134
00:08:27,960 --> 00:08:29,600
You're teaching so well,

135
00:08:31,080 --> 00:08:32,760
is the tutoring fee expensive?

136
00:08:34,360 --> 00:08:36,080
Depends on who I’m teaching.

137
00:08:37,720 --> 00:08:39,159
Some people get it for free.

138
00:08:49,400 --> 00:08:50,360
Whoa!

139
00:08:51,200 --> 00:08:53,240
How about that? Pretty cool right?

140
00:08:53,560 --> 00:08:54,720
We even won.

141
00:08:54,800 --> 00:08:56,200
See? Got MVP too.

142
00:08:56,280 --> 00:08:57,520
Cool or what?

143
00:08:58,840 --> 00:09:01,800
My, are you this good at everything then?

144
00:09:05,280 --> 00:09:06,920
Damn! I’m heading out!

145
00:09:07,360 --> 00:09:08,560
I have to submit work to the professor.

146
00:09:08,640 --> 00:09:09,920
Lock up when you leave. See you.

147
00:09:10,000 --> 00:09:10,840
Wait!

148
00:09:10,920 --> 00:09:12,000
Wait!

149
00:09:21,120 --> 00:09:22,240
Then...

150
00:09:24,080 --> 00:09:25,160
shall we...

151
00:09:26,720 --> 00:09:28,520
keep playing, just the two of us?

152
00:09:41,600 --> 00:09:43,000
(Jeno)

153
00:09:46,240 --> 00:09:47,800
(Jeno)

154
00:10:02,880 --> 00:10:03,880
Nueng.

155
00:10:03,960 --> 00:10:05,920
I saw that you haven’t had lunch yet,

156
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:08,040
so I bought you some snacks.

157
00:10:08,560 --> 00:10:09,880
And what about love?

158
00:10:18,440 --> 00:10:20,240
The people who enter your life will be

159
00:10:21,400 --> 00:10:23,640
associated with the number one throughout.

160
00:10:26,800 --> 00:10:27,880
Chat.

161
00:10:29,560 --> 00:10:30,640
Chat.

162
00:10:30,720 --> 00:10:31,800
Huh?

163
00:10:32,840 --> 00:10:35,240
Mira shouldn’t have done that to you.

164
00:10:35,920 --> 00:10:37,280
Because I think your work

165
00:10:37,360 --> 00:10:38,680
was genuinely good.

166
00:10:42,320 --> 00:10:43,640
I made the mistake myself.

167
00:10:46,360 --> 00:10:47,960
Sucking up to Chat,

168
00:10:48,840 --> 00:10:51,040
thinking of working across both teams, huh?

169
00:10:52,800 --> 00:10:54,560
Come on Chat, let’s go eat,

170
00:10:54,640 --> 00:10:55,520
the team is waiting.

171
00:10:56,200 --> 00:10:58,400
About working across two teams,

172
00:10:59,240 --> 00:11:00,480
if you don’t perform well,

173
00:11:00,560 --> 00:11:01,600
it’s not guaranteed.

174
00:11:01,680 --> 00:11:03,160
Your team passed,

175
00:11:03,720 --> 00:11:05,960
but that doesn’t mean you’re better than Team B.

176
00:11:08,760 --> 00:11:10,120
Let's not fight.

177
00:11:10,760 --> 00:11:12,440
We’re all in the same company.

178
00:11:13,920 --> 00:11:16,440
Chat, why do you even care about them?

179
00:11:16,760 --> 00:11:19,440
They’re always messing with us.

180
00:11:21,280 --> 00:11:22,200
I’ll head out first.

181
00:11:22,280 --> 00:11:23,600
maybe someone around here

182
00:11:24,080 --> 00:11:25,520
will cool down a bit.

183
00:11:26,840 --> 00:11:27,840
Chat,

184
00:11:28,200 --> 00:11:30,040
please don’t forget to enjoy your snacks.

185
00:11:30,120 --> 00:11:31,040
Mmm.

186
00:11:34,840 --> 00:11:37,240
Easy there.

187
00:11:59,960 --> 00:12:04,000
Congratulations to Team B!

188
00:12:09,560 --> 00:12:10,800
Don't tell me...

189
00:12:12,440 --> 00:12:14,240
You guys didn't pass again.

190
00:12:15,040 --> 00:12:17,400
If I pass, will I be in this condition, sis?

191
00:12:19,440 --> 00:12:20,600
It’s alright. Come on,

192
00:12:20,680 --> 00:12:21,880
I’ll treat you to a meal today.

193
00:12:22,640 --> 00:12:23,680
Come, come.

194
00:12:24,800 --> 00:12:26,480
What should we eat today?

195
00:12:27,320 --> 00:12:28,720
Come on, take a seat.

196
00:12:29,040 --> 00:12:30,440
I have no appetite, sis.

197
00:12:30,800 --> 00:12:32,360
Huh? Why is that?

198
00:12:38,000 --> 00:12:41,400
If our team’s project doesn’t pass in these three months,

199
00:12:41,480 --> 00:12:42,640
the whole team has to go.

200
00:12:43,000 --> 00:12:44,120
Huh?

201
00:12:52,160 --> 00:12:53,000
Jeez.

202
00:12:54,320 --> 00:12:57,320
So Team B better start preparing to find new jobs then.

203
00:13:00,680 --> 00:13:01,840
You’re so nosy

204
00:13:01,920 --> 00:13:04,560
about other people’s business, Namwan!

205
00:13:04,640 --> 00:13:07,760
Who knows, she might come buy your drink shop!

206
00:13:07,840 --> 00:13:08,720
Oh really?

207
00:13:08,800 --> 00:13:11,520
Maybe sell your food better first, auntie!

208
00:13:13,600 --> 00:13:14,880
Go bankrupt already!

209
00:13:14,960 --> 00:13:16,200
Use the time you spend talking

210
00:13:16,280 --> 00:13:18,440
to go find yourself a new job too!

211
00:13:21,920 --> 00:13:24,040
You don’t have to go find new jobs anywhere.

212
00:13:28,160 --> 00:13:29,840
You can come work with me.

213
00:13:30,360 --> 00:13:31,920
Team A has a lot of work,

214
00:13:32,000 --> 00:13:33,680
we happen to need more people.

215
00:13:36,040 --> 00:13:38,000
It’s not that you’re not good,

216
00:13:38,080 --> 00:13:39,200
it’s just that

217
00:13:39,600 --> 00:13:41,920
your leader isn’t good enough.

218
00:13:42,000 --> 00:13:44,240
Choose the wrong team and this is what happens!

219
00:13:48,920 --> 00:13:50,520
There are still three months.

220
00:13:50,600 --> 00:13:51,720
There’s no way

221
00:13:51,800 --> 00:13:53,680
I’m letting Team B get fired.

222
00:13:53,760 --> 00:13:55,360
You seem confident.

223
00:13:56,440 --> 00:13:59,000
Let’s hope that confidence of a team leader

224
00:13:59,640 --> 00:14:01,880
doesn’t end up causing trouble for your team members.

225
00:14:02,720 --> 00:14:04,080
We’re not going to be in trouble.

226
00:14:04,520 --> 00:14:05,880
We’ll stick around

227
00:14:05,960 --> 00:14:07,960
and be a thorn in the side of people who love to bark

228
00:14:08,720 --> 00:14:11,600
aren’t you tired of barking like a mad dog?

229
00:14:12,040 --> 00:14:13,480
You’re the one who’s barking.

230
00:14:13,560 --> 00:14:16,640
Oh acting all high and mighty saying you won’t be in trouble

231
00:14:16,720 --> 00:14:19,760
just wait until you actually get fired.

232
00:14:19,840 --> 00:14:21,280
You’ll be speechless,

233
00:14:21,680 --> 00:14:24,000
scrambling to find a new job barely in time.

234
00:14:24,640 --> 00:14:25,960
That’s enough, Tommy.

235
00:14:26,440 --> 00:14:27,840
Whatever you want to say,

236
00:14:27,920 --> 00:14:29,880
save my old friend's face a little.

237
00:14:33,400 --> 00:14:34,480
But if

238
00:14:36,000 --> 00:14:38,000
you do end up getting fired,

239
00:14:38,720 --> 00:14:40,000
you can tell me.

240
00:14:40,640 --> 00:14:42,600
I’ll go talk to Ms. Nichakorn for you.

241
00:14:58,040 --> 00:14:59,600
He doesn’t care about you.

242
00:15:02,520 --> 00:15:05,600
Team A and Team B can’t be friends.

243
00:15:06,240 --> 00:15:08,440
But you and I, we used to be friends.

244
00:15:09,080 --> 00:15:10,000
Used to be.

245
00:15:10,520 --> 00:15:12,800
But it ended the day we became rivals.

246
00:15:13,160 --> 00:15:14,320
Besides,

247
00:15:14,920 --> 00:15:16,120
what you’re hoping for,

248
00:15:16,600 --> 00:15:18,040
it will never happen

249
00:15:19,040 --> 00:15:21,440
And do you even know what I’m hoping for?

250
00:15:21,880 --> 00:15:23,680
I could tell what you were thinking

251
00:15:24,280 --> 00:15:25,600
even from the moon.

252
00:15:25,680 --> 00:15:27,200
If you already know then good,

253
00:15:27,920 --> 00:15:29,280
because if I want something,

254
00:15:29,840 --> 00:15:30,880
I will get it.

255
00:15:32,920 --> 00:15:34,080
Go ahead and try.

256
00:15:58,440 --> 00:16:00,400
At least only work fails,

257
00:16:00,480 --> 00:16:02,160
but my love life is still okay.

258
00:16:03,480 --> 00:16:07,160
(Jeno, Chat)

259
00:16:12,800 --> 00:16:14,720
(Nice to meet you)

260
00:16:30,120 --> 00:16:34,480
(Jeno, Chat)

261
00:16:35,080 --> 00:16:37,120
This is your surprise?

262
00:16:39,080 --> 00:16:40,160
Yes.

263
00:16:40,440 --> 00:16:42,240
today is our anniversary,

264
00:16:42,800 --> 00:16:44,760
so I wanted to do something

265
00:16:46,240 --> 00:16:48,800
to show you how much I love you.

266
00:16:48,880 --> 00:16:50,160
Just a lock?

267
00:16:59,760 --> 00:17:02,560
Do you know that in Korea there’s a belief that

268
00:17:03,200 --> 00:17:05,079
if you lock a padlock with someone,

269
00:17:05,680 --> 00:17:07,440
it will make your love strong

270
00:17:08,839 --> 00:17:10,359
and you’ll never break up?

271
00:17:15,760 --> 00:17:16,880
Do you believe in that?

272
00:17:20,079 --> 00:17:23,160
I’m just scared you’ll break up with me.

273
00:17:28,520 --> 00:17:29,360
Jeno.

274
00:17:30,400 --> 00:17:32,800
You know, you are my first love?

275
00:17:35,360 --> 00:17:36,800
No matter what happens,

276
00:17:36,880 --> 00:17:38,800
there’s no way I’d ever leave you.

277
00:17:40,960 --> 00:17:42,080
You said it now,

278
00:17:42,960 --> 00:17:44,360
if you leave me,

279
00:17:44,720 --> 00:17:46,200
I have nowhere to go.

280
00:17:56,480 --> 00:17:57,600
Your hand.

281
00:18:00,920 --> 00:18:01,800
Let's go.

282
00:18:07,840 --> 00:18:11,920
